The tests use `buffer.write`, `buffer.read`, `buffer.clear`, `buffer.overwrite`. `read()` returns a value by value (T). `write` takes a value. Since the buffer holds `std::string`, the storage must be able to hold T by value.

The test file includes "circular_buffer.h" and uses the template, so the class must be defined in the header (or declared in the header and defined in the cpp — but the template needs to be in the header). I'll put the whole implementation in the header.

Design: a fixed-size buffer using `std::vector<T>` or `std::unique_ptr<T[]>`. Since it's a fixed size, use a vector with `size` elements, plus read_pos, write_pos, count... Actually, a simpler approach: use `std::vector<T>` as storage, and track `read_`, `write_`, `size_` (capacity), and `count_`.

But wait — the tests construct with `circular_buffer<int> buffer(1)`. A constructor taking an int.

Implementation:

```cpp
#if !defined(CIRCULAR_BUFFER_H)
#define CIRCULAR_BUFFER_H

#include <stdexcept>
#include <vector>

namespace circular_buffer {

template <typename T>
class circular_buffer {
public:
    explicit circular_buffer(std::size_t capacity)
        : capacity_(capacity), read_(0), write_(0), count_(0), storage_(capacity) {}

    T read() {
        if (count_ == 0) {
            throw std::domain_error("Buffer is empty");
        }
        T value = std::move(storage_[read_]);
        read_ = (read_ + 1) % capacity_;
        --count_;
        return value;
    }

    void write(const T& value) {
        if (count_ == capacity_) {
            throw std::domain_error("Buffer is full");
        }
        overwrite(value);
    }

    void overwrite(const T& value) {
        if (count_ == capacity_) {
            storage_[write_] = value;
            write_ = (write_ + 1) % capacity_;
            read_ = (read_ + 1) % capacity_;
        } else {
            storage_[write_] = value;
            write_ = (write_ + 1) % capacity_;
            ++count_;
        }
    }

    void clear() {
        read_ = 0;
        write_ = 0;
        count_ = 0;
    }

private:
    std::size_t capacity_;
    std::size_t read_;
    std::size_t write_;
    std::size_t count_;
    std::vector<T> storage_;
};

}  // namespace circular_buffer

#endif // CIRCULAR_BUFFER_H
